# Component with the bug

`DualStorageRouter.reconcileCategoryWithPathGuard` (in `src/storage/dualStorageRouter.ts`), the method that guards `reconcile()`/`reconcileCategory()` calls using a per-category "last known md root" meta key (`md_root:<category>`).

## Old (buggy) behavior

On a category's **first-ever sighting** — i.e. when `knownRoot === null` (no recorded md root yet for that category) — the code only recorded the current resolved root via `this.vectorDb.setMeta(metaKey, resolvedRoot)` and then **fell through** to the normal (destructive) strict-mirror reconcile path (`reconcileCategory`), instead of returning early.

This was safe under the pre-ticket-06 assumption that every category reaching this method had already been reconciled at least once (categories in `md`/`split` mode never changed shape between runs). But once ticket 06 made `categories.<name>.storage` always-live (no longer gated behind `storage.mode: split`), a category could newly enter the markdown-reconciled set (`mdCategories()`) for the very first time on a store that *already had real vector rows* for it (e.g. flipping an override from `vector` to `md`, or removing a previously-ignored `categories.foo.storage: vector` override). In that case the category's `.md` file had never been written, so the destructive mirror read it as empty and deleted every corresponding vector row as "absent from markdown" — real, silent data loss.

## New (fixed) behavior

The first-ever-sighting branch (`knownRoot === null`) is now merged with the "root changed" branch: both cases call `seedCategoryFromVector(category)` to re-export/reseed the category's markdown from the vector index (the authoritative source), record the new root via `setMeta`, and `return` immediately — never falling through to the destructive mirror on that call. For a genuinely brand-new category (nothing in either store yet) this reseed is just a harmless zero-row export. The next call then reconciles normally against a now-populated `.md` file.

```ts
// before
if (knownRoot === null) {
  this.vectorDb.setMeta(metaKey, resolvedRoot);
} else if (knownRoot !== resolvedRoot) {
  await this.seedCategoryFromVector(category);
  this.vectorDb.setMeta(metaKey, resolvedRoot);
  return;
}

// after
if (knownRoot === null || knownRoot !== resolvedRoot) {
  await this.seedCategoryFromVector(category);
  this.vectorDb.setMeta(metaKey, resolvedRoot);
  return;
}
```

This fix was made in commit `08fbdda2` ("feat(config): storage mode top-level default with per-category override, remove split", ticket 06, neuron-2.3.0), discovered while making the per-category storage override always-live instead of conditional on `storage.mode: split`.
